  "Software" means this work in all the forms in which it is distributed: the interpreter Pymo in Python (pymo/), the
  interpreter Haskimo in Haskell (haskimo/), the standard library (lib/), the system documents (docs/), the examples, the tests, the
  documentation, and every file of the distribution that carries or is covered by this license.
  "Author" means the copyright holder named above.
  "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.
  "Derivative Work" means any work based on the Software: a modification, translation or port (also to another programming language or
  notation), and any work that contains a part of the Software or is combined with it so that the two are distributed as one program or
  library.  A program written in the i-1 language is a Derivative Work if it is distributed together with the Software or with a part of it
  (for example with files of lib/).  A program that is distributed alone and is merely run by the Software is not, and neither is the text
  that the Software prints when it runs.
  "Convey" means to make a copy of the Software or of a Derivative Work available to anyone else, by any means, with or without charge.
  "Corresponding Source" of a work means its complete source code in the form preferred for making changes (for this Software: the .imo
  files in every notation, the Python and Haskell files, the generated files that are part of the distribution, the build, installation,
  generation and test scripts),
  and everything needed to understand, build, run and test it.
  "Non-Commercial Purpose" means a purpose that is not primarily intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage or monetary
  compensation.  Private study, hobby use, teaching and learning, academic and other research whose results are published openly, and use
  by charities, schools, universities and public bodies for their non-commercial tasks are Non-Commercial Purposes.  The following are NOT:
  use in or for a product or service that is sold, licensed or offered for a fee or other consideration; use by or for a for-profit
  organization in the course of its business, including internal use, consulting, contract work and paid training; use that produces revenue
  (advertising, subscriptions, sale of data or results); offering the Software or a Derivative Work as a paid or hosted service.  A
  voluntary donation toward a Derivative Work that is conveyed free of charge does not make it commercial; a payment for the Software or a
  Derivative Work, or for access to it, does.

